    "explanation": "This dispute is over the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee shown on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02742), and it turns on whether all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold. They do. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 18:35:49. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02742) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:35:49, and it holds 19 qualifying in-radius fixes, so the arrival test of POL-NS-02 is met; the arrival marker's own timestamp coincides with that fix, so POL-NS-05 finds no false marker to correct. (c) The continuous in-geofence dwell runs from that first qualifying fix at 18:35:49 to the cancellation at 18:38:50, i.e. 181 seconds against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). POL-NS-01(c) expressly measures the dwell from the first qualifying GPS fix and not from the 'arrived' event or the platform wait timer, so the submission that the wait-timer start at 18:35:51 leaves a 179-second shortfall is declined: the wrong clock was used. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 18:38:50 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, at or after the moment the dwell elapsed. The rider's other routes do not open. POL-NS-06 has no shortfall to operate on, because the effective in-geofence dwell (181 s) exceeds the minimum; POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m radius, not in the 50-400 m wrong-entrance band; POL-NS-04 does not exonerate, because the only chat message is the driver's own, sent 18:36:09, and the rider's 46 fixes sit 622-630 m from the pin, outside the 100 m rider-presence radius. The traffic advisory that POL-NS-06(i) requires before separate in-geofence intervals may be summed is MISSING (EV-ADVIS-02742-01, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, disclosed by both sides), so no outside-radius time can be recovered - which changes nothing here, because the driver's dwell is a single unbroken in-geofence run. The fee therefore stands, and POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of SGD 4.50, which is SGD 3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0, below the threshold of 4, so compensation is payable rather than withheld. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd; the rider's charge itself is left as it stands and is not a second payment. Confidence is capped at 1.0, the weight of the GPS trace and trip record that carry the deciding facts. No clause produces a referral: the arrival marker was not false under POL-NS-05(ii), the RIDER_NO_SHOW code was correctly selected, and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met (the two-second difference between the wait-timer start and the GPS dwell start is well inside POL-NS-08(a), and POL-NS-01(c) resolves which clock governs). The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling executes automatically, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
