    "explanation": "Both parties: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee stands, and the driver is to be paid SGD 3.60 as compensation. Per POL-GEN-03, on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd carries the same figure as driver_compensation_sgd; it is the money this ruling moves, not a refund to the rider.\n\nPOL-NS-01 requires all four of its conditions and each one holds on this record. (a) EV-TRIP-02742 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 18:35:49. (b) EV-GPS-02742 places the driver inside the STANDARD-zone 50 m arrival radius from 18:35:49 onward — 19 qualifying in-radius fixes at accuracy inside the 25 m filter. (c) The driver held position continuously from 18:35:49 to the 18:38:50 cancellation: a dwell of 181 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is null). POL-NS-01(c) measures that dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and expressly not from the 'arrived' event, so 18:35:49→18:38:50, i.e. 181 seconds, is the operative figure; the trace's own shortfall figure is −1.0 second, a surplus. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 18:38:50 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell had elapsed (18:35:49 + 180s = 18:38:49).\n\nThe rider's two arguments are answered and rejected on their merits. First, the rider points to the platform wait timer, which started at 18:35:51 and ran 179 seconds to cancellation with no wait_timer_expired event. That does not decide limb (c): the clause fixes the measure at the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not at the platform's wait timer or the arrival tap, and the GPS clock gives 181 seconds. The two-second difference is far inside POL-NS-08(a)'s 90-second skew threshold and is resolved by POL-NS-01(c) itself, so it is not a POL-NS-09(b) contradiction. Second, the rider argues a one-second margin should not be read generously. The clause states a minimum, not a discretionary range; 181 ≥ 180 is met and there is no licence to raise the requirement.\n\nNo clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. POL-NS-03 does not open: the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 has no foothold: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02742) contains only the driver's message, so limb (a) fails, and the rider track holds no fix inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, so limb (c) fails on admissible fixes. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: dwell_start_offset_sec is 0.0, the arrival marker coincides with the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and no false marker stands to be recomputed. POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall, and its accumulation limb (i) is not needed, the driver's dwell being one unbroken run; the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02742-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed and named, but it carries no deciding fact and so neither caps confidence nor escalates the case.\n\nPOL-NS-07 fixes the payout at 80 percent of the net fee in force: 0.80 × 4.50 = 3.60 SGD. The anti-farming guard does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0, below the '4 or more' threshold, and no other profile field is used. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08: no clock skew, no sampling gap (0.0 s maximum, 100 percent coverage), the chat log matches trip_record.chat_message_count, and the fare line of 4.50 reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. No clause produces a referral (there is no false-arrival finding under POL-NS-05(ii), no billing-integrity finding under POL-RD-09(4), and no driver-conduct item), so the referrals list is empty. Confidence is set at 0.90, below the 1.0 cap carried by the weight-1.0 artifacts that decide the case, and above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation arises. The monetary effect of 3.60 SGD is below the 8.00 SGD execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue."
